---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Why Money in Austria exists, who it's for, and how to use it: plain-English financial guidance for immigrants living in Austria."
  path="/about/"
>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hero">
      <span class="badge">About</span>
      <h1>Financial paperwork shouldn't be another language barrier.</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="prose" style="padding-block: 1rem 3rem;">
      <p>
        Moving to Austria means learning a new financial system, often in a language
        you're still learning too. Payslips, tax letters, and insurance forms use
        precise German terms that don't always translate cleanly, and getting them
        wrong can be expensive or stressful.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Money in Austria</strong> is a plain-English guide to how money
        works here: taxes, social insurance, banking, pensions, family benefits,
        and investing. Every article explains German terms the first time they appear,
        so you build a working vocabulary as you read.
      </p>

      <h2>Who this is for</h2>
      <p>
        Anyone who has recently moved to Austria and wants to understand their
        payslip, tax return, insurance card, or first bank account, without wading
        through government legalese or forum threads of mixed advice.
      </p>

      <h2>What this isn't</h2>
      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          Money in Austria is informational only and does not constitute financial, tax, or
          legal advice. Rules change and individual situations vary, so always confirm
          details with a qualified <em lang="de">Steuerberater</em> (tax advisor), your
          social insurance provider, or the relevant Austrian authority before making
          decisions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Feedback</h2>
      <p>
        This is a small, independent project. If something is unclear or out of date,
        we'd rather know than have it sit wrong on the page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
